        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "0.227 g H4PMIDA (1.0 mmol), 0.249 g Ni(CH3COO)2·4H2O (1.0 mmol) and 2.0 mL Gd(ClO4)3 (0.5 M) were dissolved in 10 mL deionized water. The pH was adjusted with 1 M NaOH to 5.0–5.5, giving a cloudy aqueous mixture that was sealed in an 18 mL Teflon-lined Parr autoclave, heated at 180 °C for 100 h, then cooled to room temperature at 4 °C h−1. The mixture was filtered and the filtrate was evaporated at room temperature for two weeks to give light-green needle-shaped crystals.",
